UID:d14-caso-vmageste-en-biblioteca-2026-10@lagrotti.dev
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Read the flow before choosing the tool
DESCRIPTION:LinkedIn\n\nRead the flow before choosing the tool\n\nEvent dis
 cussions become more concrete when we draw the stages: where data enters\,
  where it is processed and how it reaches queries. The VMAGeste case study
  uses that flow as an entry point into its architecture decisions.\n\nMy s
 uggested reading exercise: identify an asynchronous boundary\, write down 
 the assumption it addresses and look for what operations would need to obs
 erve. Use the case for context and the library demo to test capacity ideas
  with synthetic data.\n\nWhat do you look for first in a diagram when tryi
 ng to understand failure recovery?\n\nhttps://lagrotti.dev/en/projetos/vma
 geste?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=biblioteca-2026-1
 0&utm_content=d14-caso-vmageste-en
URL:https://lagrotti.dev/en/projetos/vmageste?utm_source=linkedin&utm_mediu
 m=social&utm_campaign=biblioteca-2026-10&utm_content=d14-caso-vmageste-en
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d15-oficina-en-biblioteca-2026-10@lagrotti.dev
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:One hour to write a defensible decision
DESCRIPTION:LinkedIn\n\nOne hour to write a defensible decision\n\nI prepar
 ed a self-guided workshop around one bounded problem: 20 orders/s arrive\,
  two are processed per second and the burst lasts ten seconds. The task is
  to model backlog and record a decision in an ADR.\n\nThe outline splits o
 ne hour between context\, experiment\, alternatives\, writing and review. 
 Work alone or in pairs with only a browser and text editor. The material i
 ncludes exercises\, expected outcomes and an answer key for discussion.\n\
 nThis is available material\, with no registration or scheduled event. Whi
 ch condition would make you reject work instead of queuing it?\n\nhttps://
 lagrotti.dev/en/recursos/campanhas/oficina-arquitetura?utm_source=linkedin
 &utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=biblioteca-2026-10&utm_content=d15-oficina
 -en
URL:https://lagrotti.dev/en/recursos/campanhas/oficina-arquitetura?utm_sour
 ce=linkedin&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=biblioteca-2026-10&utm_content=
 d15-oficina-en
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
