UID:d16-pico-en-biblioteca-2026-10@lagrotti.dev
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Two-minute challenge
DESCRIPTION:WhatsApp\n\nTwo-minute challenge\n\n20 arrivals/s\, two workers
 \, 0% failures\, ten seconds. How much work remains? Predict before openin
 g the demo\, then stop arrivals to measure recovery. The exercise separate
 s a temporary burst from a permanent capacity deficit.\n\nhttps://lagrotti
 .dev/en/recursos/laboratorio/sobrecarga?utm_source=whatsapp&utm_medium=mes
 saging&utm_campaign=biblioteca-2026-10&utm_content=d16-pico-en
URL:https://lagrotti.dev/en/recursos/laboratorio/sobrecarga?utm_source=what
 sapp&utm_medium=messaging&utm_campaign=biblioteca-2026-10&utm_content=d16-
 pico-en
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d17-adr-review-en-biblioteca-2026-10@lagrotti.dev
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261104
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261105
SUMMARY:ADR review: what evidence would change your decision?
DESCRIPTION:Developer community\n\nADR review: what evidence would change y
 our decision?\n\nAn exercise for an architecture discussion: use the self-
 guided workshop scenario and write an ADR with context\, two alternatives\
 , a decision\, consequences and a review condition. Avoid justifying it th
 rough tool preference alone.\n\nOne alternative can retain current capacit
 y and accept delay\; another can increase workers or reject arrivals above
  a limit. Compare recovery time\, cost\, duplication and user-visible beha
 vior. State the assumptions your experiment did not measure.\n\nDuring rev
 iew\, look for a testable condition that would force reconsideration. The 
 material includes an example answer without treating one architecture as t
 he only solution. Which assumption is missing from your ADR?\n\nhttps://la
 grotti.dev/en/recursos/campanhas/oficina-arquitetura?utm_source=community&
 utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=biblioteca-2026-10&utm_content=d17-adr-revi
 ew-en
URL:https://lagrotti.dev/en/recursos/campanhas/oficina-arquitetura?utm_sour
 ce=community&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=biblioteca-2026-10&utm_content
 =d17-adr-review-en
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d18-monolito-en-biblioteca-2026-10@lagrotti.dev
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261105
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261106
SUMMARY:Does a code boundary need to become a service?
DESCRIPTION:LinkedIn\n\nDoes a code boundary need to become a service?\n\nS
 eparating responsibilities is one decision\; separating deployments is ano
 ther. A boundary can begin inside a modular monolith and later gain indepe
 ndent operations if a concrete need emerges.\n\nThe guide on modular monol
 iths and separate services compares autonomy\, contracts and operating cos
 t. A new process also adds networking\, observability and partial failures
 .\n\nBefore splitting\, write down the constraint that separation solves a
 nd the condition that would justify revisiting it. Which part of your syst
 em needs operational autonomy today?\n\nhttps://lagrotti.dev/en/recursos/g
 uias/monolito?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=bibliotec
 a-2026-10&utm_content=d18-monolito-en
URL:https://lagrotti.dev/en/recursos/guias/monolito?utm_source=linkedin&utm
 _medium=social&utm_campaign=biblioteca-2026-10&utm_content=d18-monolito-en
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
