UID:d21-caso-pulsewatch-en-biblioteca-2026-10@lagrotti.dev
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:What should you observe beyond queue length?
DESCRIPTION:LinkedIn\n\nWhat should you observe beyond queue length?\n\nTwo
  backlogs of the same size can represent very different situations. A queu
 e that drains quickly after a burst calls for one interpretation\; an old 
 message that never progresses calls for another.\n\nTo explore that differ
 ence\, read the PulseWatch case alongside the queue guide. Use the case as
  product and operations context without turning simulator numbers into pro
 ject metrics.\n\nIn your review\, note three signals: oldest message age\,
  completion rate and failure destination. Which signal would help you choo
 se between waiting\, scaling and investigating?\n\nhttps://lagrotti.dev/en
 /projetos/pulsewatch?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=bi
 blioteca-2026-10&utm_content=d21-caso-pulsewatch-en
URL:https://lagrotti.dev/en/projetos/pulsewatch?utm_source=linkedin&utm_med
 ium=social&utm_campaign=biblioteca-2026-10&utm_content=d21-caso-pulsewatch
 -en
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d22-retries-en-biblioteca-2026-10@lagrotti.dev
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261110
SUMMARY:Where does the third failure go?
DESCRIPTION:LinkedIn\n\nWhere does the third failure go?\n\nA retry needs a
  limit and a destination after that limit. In the educational demo\, a mes
 sage failing three times goes to a dead-letter queue. That ends the model'
 s automatic cycle but does not explain how to fix the cause.\n\nAn operati
 ons discussion must say who investigates\, how to identify the message and
  when replay is safe. Moving work from an endless retry loop into an unown
 ed error store is not enough.\n\nThe glossary explains DLQs and connects t
 he concept to the exercise. If a message reached the dead-letter queue tod
 ay\, would your team know the next step?\n\nhttps://lagrotti.dev/en/recurs
 os/glossario/dead-letter?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=social&utm_campaig
 n=biblioteca-2026-10&utm_content=d22-retries-en
URL:https://lagrotti.dev/en/recursos/glossario/dead-letter?utm_source=linke
 din&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=biblioteca-2026-10&utm_content=d22-retr
 ies-en
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
