DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261113
SUMMARY:From payload to product context
DESCRIPTION:LinkedIn\n\nFrom payload to product context\n\nA diff shows tha
 t a field changed. Deciding whether it matters needs context: who produces
  it\, who consumes it and which behavior depends on it.\n\nUse the Eurolog
 ado case study as a reading exercise. Pick one described flow and write a 
 minimal fictional contract for it. Then add a field and change a value usi
 ng the library's JSON comparator.\n\nThis does not reproduce the project's
  internal contracts. It connects a comparison tool to product questions: c
 an the consumer tolerate the change? Would validation detect an incompatib
 ility?\n\nhttps://lagrotti.dev/en/projetos/eurologado?utm_source=linkedin&
 utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=biblioteca-2026-10&utm_content=d25-caso-eur
 ologado-en
